WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.690
Luffy’s biggest failure was letting his
brother Ace die during the war at Marineford.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:10.370
But since that catastrophic defeat, Luffy
has grown into one of the strongest characters

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.970
in the story.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:18.850
Which makes me wonder, could Luffy have saved
Ace if he had ALL of his powers from the current

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:19.850
story?

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:25.500
So in this video, we are going to give Luffy
a chance to see if he can turn this [show

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.090
Ace dying with Akainu’s fist] into this
[show thumbnail again].

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:32.960
To start things off, just like in the original
story Luffy arrives after the battle has already

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.120
started.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.590
And basically everything leading up the war
remains the same.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:01:01.240
The Whitebeard pirates have clashed with the
marines and Luffy is falling towards Whitebeard’s

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:19.780
ship.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:02:09.300
Only 

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.770
this time, the former strongest man alive
senses that Luffy is not just some random

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.380
kid falling from the sky.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:22.180
Instead, Whitebeard senses a threat and swings
his blade with a fully charged conqueror’s

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:25.459
haki blast just like he did against Roger.

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:30.910
Luffy blocks with his own conqueror’s infused
sandals, and their epic clash splits the skies

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.189
[can you make something like when roger clashed
with whitebeard in ch 966].

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:38.920
After this initial clash, they quickly figure
out that they are both here to save Ace and

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.010
decide to team up, just like they did in the
original Marineford.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:49.310
But before we see how Gear 5 Luffy would completely
flip this battle on its head, you might want

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:55.080
to ask, Manu, how in the world would it even
be possible for Luffy to have awakened Gear

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.319
5 this early in the story?

00:02:57.319 --> 00:02:59.490
Well, there are few plausible options.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:03.610
For example, Luffy could have unlocked Gear
5 after nearly dying in underwater prison

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.610
Impel Down.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:09.470
Or he could have met someone else in the Grand
Line who taught him the secrets of his devil

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.470
fruit.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.220
But since the main point of this video is
to see how current storyline Luffy would do

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.270
at Marineford, I’ll say ‘don’t worry
about it’.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:22.989
We’ll just assume that he has awakened his
fruit SOMEHOW, that Ace is still captured,

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:27.590
and that everything else is basically the
same from the original story.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:34.360
Because, as you’d expect, just this one
change alone is going to make the outcome

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.560
insanely different.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.799
This time Luffy will have no trouble getting
past the common marines and vice-admirals.

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:44.980
With a single blast of conqueror’s haki,
he knocks out most of the marines and heads

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.450
right for his brother Ace.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:51.659
And in this version of the war, Luffy will
likely still clash with the strongest swordsman

00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:53.379
in the world, Mihawk.

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:57.480
Originally, the warlord wanted to test himself
against Whitebeard, so he would definitely

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.140
want to clash against this overpowered Luffy.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.379
So can Mihawk take on the awakened Luffy?

00:04:04.379 --> 00:04:16.830
We know that Mihawk is an overpowered swordsman,
and swords are basically Luffy’s main weakness.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:21.720
But one thing you have to consider is that
Luffy would be showing off his Gear 5 powers

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.150
for the first time.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.810
And just like we witnessed during the Wano
arc, seeing Gear 5 Luffy for the first time

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.300
can make anyone seem silly [show luffy jump
roping with Kaido in ch 1045].

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.060
So when Mihawk swings his giant sword, Luffy
blocks it with Advanced Conqueror's haki,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:41.400
grabs Mihawk by the cape, and swings him around
like a little tornado [kinda like tasmanian

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.290
devil from looney toons].

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.370
Mihawk responds with a flurry of slashes,
but at this point the Whitebeard commander

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:54.120
Vista jumps in [similar to ch 561] so Luffy
can continue towards Ace.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.490
Meanwhile, everyone watching this clash is
stunned.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:01.490
Ace is shocked that his brother is so powerful.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:06.780
The marines are in awe of this ridiculous
power that they have never seen before.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:12.740
Even whitebeard, who out of everyone here
possibly knows that most about the void century,

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:18.810
can’t believe that this kid he has never
heard of has such insane powers.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:24.560
As always, Luffy doesn’t care about what
others think, he is simply focused on freeing

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.050
his brother, no matter who stands in his way.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:33.090
But first, let’s recap all of the powers
that Luffy didn’t have at the original Marineford

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.390
war [consider a checklist here].

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:40.930
He now has mastery over every form of Gear
4 such as Bound man, Tank man, and Snake man

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:44.199
that he learned while training with Rayleigh
during the time skip.

00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:49.340
He also mastered Future Sight Haki during
his fight with the mochi man, Katakuri, and

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:55.900
in Wano he learned both Advanced Armament
while in prison AND advanced conquerors haki

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.090
during his fight with the Emperor Kaido.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:05.290
On top of all that, during that same fight
with Kaido, he finally awakened Gear 5.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:11.360
And while the Gear 5 powers can look goofy
at first, the awakened form of Luffy’s devil

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.930
fruit literally allows him to make his imagination
reality.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:19.419
This explains his fire powers such as Red
Hawk and Red Roc.

00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:22.770
And also the impossible ways he can bend his
body.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:29.470
And since Luffy is THE MOST creative character
we have seen in One Piece, the possibilities

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:32.660
for his new powers seem almost endless.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:39.210
With so many new powers, it seems like Luffy
should wipe the floor with everyone at Marineford,

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.270
right?

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:42.380
Not quite.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:49.190
We also have to consider how the marines might
act differently if Luffy showed so much power.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:55.990
First, we will assume that the admirals would
know at least Armament and Observation Haki,

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:01.720
and probably advanced armament since they
even seemed to show it when they blocked Whitebeard’s

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.759
shock waves at the original marineford [ch
564].

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:09.460
It is also extremely likely that the admirals
Aokiji, the Chilly fruit logia user, and Akainu,

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:15.120
the Magma fruit user, have unlocked their
devil fruit awakening.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:19.750
While we don’t really know, we’ve already
seen what could be their awakened powers on

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.840
Punk Hazard, where they changed the landscape
of the island permanently [ch 658 or episode

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:25.840
583].

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.960
So while Oda wasn’t ready to reveal these
powers during the original war at Marineford,

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:35.240
it seems fair that the admirals would use
it now since we already know what awakening

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:36.440
is from Luffy.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:41.430
Plus the admirals didn’t really consider
Luffy a threat back at Marineford, but this

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:46.940
time around he would be one of their main
targets.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:54.470
As the battle fully begins, Luffy is confronted
by both Aokiji and the light fruit user, Kizaru.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:58.530
Their combined powers should keep Luffy contained
for now.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.430
But keep watching to see if they can actually
keep Luffy from freeing Ace.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:10.400
But Luffy isn’t the only top-tier fighter
here or the only one with a broken devil fruit.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:15.470
In a previous video about all the devil fruits
in One Piece, we talked about how Whitebeard’s

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.860
Tremor fruit has the power to literally destroy
islands.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:24.020
And Akainu’s Magma fruit is confirmed to
be the most destructive devil fruit in the

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.500
entire story.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:31.120
Well in this scenario, these two would still
clash just like they did in the original Marineford

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.120
[ch 567].

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.830
That leaves the other warlords like the string
fruit user, Doflamingo, and the shadow fruit

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:40.940
user, Gecko Moria, to fight against the Whitebeard
commanders and the prisoners from Impel down.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:46.300
But this particular part of the battle is
much different now that Luffy is fighting

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:52.660
two of the admirals by himself, meaning Aokiji
and Kizaru cannot help fight against the Whitebeard

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:53.660
pirates.

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:59.670
So the warlords would quickly be overrun,
meaning that fleet admiral Sengoku would probably

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.839
order Luffy’s grandpa Garp and the cyborg
Pacifista to enter the battle to support the

00:09:04.839 --> 00:09:05.880
marines.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.310
Another important change would be that since
Whitebeard joined the fight earlier, Squard,

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:16.630
an allied captain of Whitebeard, never had
the chance to betray him [ch 562].

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:22.010
This means that Whitebeard would be even stronger
than we saw him in the original war.

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:26.260
Even the encircling wall that the marines
used as a trap would be meaningless because

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:29.339
Luffy could just punch his own holes in it.

00:09:29.339 --> 00:09:34.190
So far, things are not going well for the
marines.

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:37.190
Which would definitely lead to Akainu doing
something desperate.

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:42.870
If the battle was going so poorly, I think
he would likely use his awakening to change

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.899
the battlefield into magma.

00:09:44.899 --> 00:09:49.540
It would literally be like the floor is lava.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:54.110
But the allies have ways to counter this.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:59.010
Whitebeard could use his tremor powers to
make a tidal wave that would cool the magma.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:04.170
Luffy could even use Gear 5 to do something
silly like blow super cold air onto the molten

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.170
rock.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:06.680
Now, let’s jump back to Luffy.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:12.380
While Aokiji and Kizaru have done a good job
keeping him busy, at some point I think the

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:18.269
Phoenix fruit user, Marco, who is the strongest
Whitebeard commander, would come to help him.

00:10:18.269 --> 00:10:21.000
This would allow Luffy time to get away.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.540
So Luffy would reach the platform where his
brother Ace is tied in chains.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:28.740
The fleet admiral Sengoku is still waiting
for him here.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:33.750
But with Luffy this strong I don’t think
the golden Buddah would be able to keep Luffy

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:34.959
from freeing his brother.

00:10:34.959 --> 00:10:40.180
And with Luffy’s future sight, Kizaru wouldn’t
be able to snipe the key [ch 571], meaning

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:42.820
Luffy would set Ace free.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:47.470
Then they just fly away and everyone is safe
right???

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:48.910
Hardly.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.600
Freeing Ace was the easy part.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:56.190
Now we’ll need to see if everyone can get
out alive.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:02.650
While Ace is free, Whitebeard and Akainu have
both taken considerable damage.

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:10.250
Marco is struggling with Kizaru and Aokiji,
Garp, Mihawk, and the Pacifista are overwhelming

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:13.340
the Impel Down prisoners and the Whitebeard
commanders.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:15.250
The pirates are beginning to break.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.720
But with Luffy and Ace back in the battle,
everyone gets a giant boost in morale.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:26.090
And Luffy can even show Ace his own fire powers
such as Red Hawk and Red Roc.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:31.300
The allies start to return to their ships,
but just like the original in Marineford,

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.250
Akainu targets the reunited brothers.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:38.340
Kizaru takes over fighting the Whitebeard
and Akainu confronts Ace and Luffy.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:43.830
Akainu would probably tempt Ace with insults
just like he did in the original war, still

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:48.560
being the hot-head that he is would turn back
to fight Akainu.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.300
But the admiral is still stronger.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:58.240
He knocks Ace to the ground with a magma covered
fist then stands over him to land the death

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.240
blow.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.620
But this time Luffy isn’t helpless.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:07.950
Instead he appears behind Akainu, and with
a furious roar, punches a hole straight through

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.269
the magma man.

00:12:09.269 --> 00:12:11.930
Damn, that was satisfying.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:17.260
And while Ace died from a similar wound in
the original story, we don’t know if Luffy

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.870
can actually defeat Akainu even with his current
powers.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:26.150
For example, Akainu could use future sight
and then morph his body around Luffy’s punch,

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:31.400
similar to what Katakuri did with his mochi
powers [ch 884].

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:38.779
Regardless, this would stop Akainu from killing
Ace and give Whitebeard enough time to arrive

00:12:38.779 --> 00:12:42.940
and CRUSH Akainu with an ISLAND SHATTERING
PUNCH.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:47.100
Which leaves Akainu laying on the rock in
a bloody heap.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:52.850
Cracks form in the island as the brothers
and Whitebeard get away, joyfully laughing

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.519
because of their freedom.

00:12:54.519 --> 00:12:56.430
But the battle still rages on.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:59.720
And it’s now that the cruelest antagonist
finally arrives.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:00.959
That’s right.

00:13:00.959 --> 00:13:03.970
Blackbeard has joined the party.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:08.649
With his haunting laughter echoing across
the field, Blackbeard and his new crew look

00:13:08.649 --> 00:13:10.370
down on the battlefield.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:15.660
Remember that Blackbeard was the cause of
this whole war when he captured Ace and brought

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:16.880
him to the Marines.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:22.050
He did this to become a Warlord and gain access
to the underwater prison Impel Down so he

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:25.339
could gather a powerful crew from the imprisoned
criminals.

00:13:25.339 --> 00:13:32.279
And he came to Marineford intending to kill
Whitebeard and steal his devil fruit.

00:13:32.279 --> 00:13:36.530
Well this time around, things are completely
different.

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:38.149
Ace is alive.

00:13:38.149 --> 00:13:40.399
Luffy is a monster.

00:13:40.399 --> 00:13:43.000
And Whitebeard is no longer on death’s door.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:48.220
So while it is certainly possible that Blackbeard
would see this situation and decide it isn’t

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:54.209
worth the risk, to keep things more interesting
let’s assume that Blackbeard chooses to

00:13:54.209 --> 00:13:55.509
continue his plan.

00:13:55.509 --> 00:13:58.880
He and his crew immediately focus on Whitebeard.

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.931
While Whitebeard might not be a walking corpse
like he was in the original battle, he has

00:14:02.931 --> 00:14:08.410
still suffered a lot of damage fighting Akainu.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:13.800
The Yonko and the darkness fruit user clash
and Whitebeard is almost defeated.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:19.370
But then Ace and Luffy leap in front to protect
the old man.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:24.089
At this point, Sengoku arrives, crushing the
Blackbeard crew just like in the original

00:14:24.089 --> 00:14:25.089
war [ch 578].

00:14:25.089 --> 00:14:30.740
This gives Marco time to come over and heal
Whitebeard, and unlike his usual brash attitude,

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:34.300
Ace begs Whitebeard to retreat so that he
can live.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:40.660
Whitebeard agrees, and signals the retreat,
but only after adding one last insult to the

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:45.040
world government by proclaiming that the One
Piece is real [ch 576].

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.279
The marines are stunned.

00:14:47.279 --> 00:14:52.320
The allied pirates pull back, ready to return
home with a complete victory.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.630
But the battle is not done yet.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:15:00.641
Akainu returns and continues to attack with
the full force of the other admirals, Because

00:15:00.641 --> 00:15:04.310
at this point the marines are about to suffer
a humiliating defeat.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:10.470
So even if Sengoku ordered the admirals to
stay back, Akainu would likely refuse to stop

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.610
because he can’t stand to let the Marine’s
honor be tarnished.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:20.470
So the battle continues with Akainu trying
to take on the pirates by himself.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:26.310
More lives are lost on both sides, and then
we get Koby’s moment of pleading to stop

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:27.310
the fighting.

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:31.360
At this moment, it is entirely likely Akainu
would not hesitate at all.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:39.430
He could kill Koby in an instant, but let’s
assume that the last main player finally arrives.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:45.050
Just like in the original war, Shanks shows
up to put an end to the fighting [ch 579,580].

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.589
This time however, Akainu goes all out at
Shanks.

00:15:48.589 --> 00:15:52.480
He cannot stand to see another pirate making
demands of the marines.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:58.720
And while we don’t know how this battle
would go, it is likely Akainu would be defeated

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.660
by the combined force of the Red Hair pirates
main officers.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:08.240
And Akainu would only live if the other admirals
saved him by pulling him back..

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:13.580
At this point, there is no doubt Blackbeard
would retreat as he didn’t even want to

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:15.500
face Shanks in the original war.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:18.870
But now we have an interesting situation.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:23.360
Luffy and Shanks meet on the battlefield as
they protect the retreating pirates.

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:30.000
And Shanks would HAVE TO now fulfill the promise
he made back in chapter 1 and fully acknowledge

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.170
Luffy as a great pirate.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:37.230
The Red Hair pirates cheer at the reunion
and there is laughter all around as the pirates

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.930
pull away from Marineford.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:44.620
It truly is a complete victory for Luffy,
but one that leaves us with so many changes

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:46.779
to the story going forward.

00:16:46.779 --> 00:16:47.779
Just listen to this.

00:16:47.779 --> 00:16:52.880
Since Ace and Whitebeard are alive, we have
to consider what they would do next.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:55.649
Whitebeard originally wanted Ace to become
the pirate king.

00:16:55.649 --> 00:17:01.010
So after this battle it is possible that Luffy
and Ace would become rivals as they search

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:02.720
the New World for the One Piece.

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:09.780
On the other hand, Ace could say he doesn’t
want to follow in his father’s footsteps,

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.520
and he could support Luffy instead.

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:17.440
Shanks could also decide to go after the One
Piece, just like he chose to do at the end

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:19.910
of Wano when he first saw Luffy’s awakened
form.

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.500
So get ready for the race to find Laugh Tale.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:27.309
But that’s not even close to the biggest
change that we will discuss at the end of

00:17:27.309 --> 00:17:28.309
this video.

00:17:28.309 --> 00:17:33.980
In fact, these changes at Marineford would
also mean that Blackbeard’s future is way

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:34.980
different.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:39.440
Now he only has one devil fruit, and he might
not even know that it is possible to collect

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.530
two of them.

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:48.230
And after seeing Luffy’s powers, could Blackbeard
target Luffy to try to get his devil fruit?

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:50.830
Could we see them clash in the new world?

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:56.260
Or would Blackbeard struggle to even become
an Emperor since he doesn’t have Whitebeard’s

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.710
devil fruit?

00:17:57.710 --> 00:18:01.370
But the biggest change would come within the
Straw Hats themselves.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:07.679
At his current power level, Luffy definitely
wouldn’t need to train, so goodbye timeskip

00:18:07.679 --> 00:18:08.791
[possibly dump volume 61 in the trash].

00:18:08.791 --> 00:18:12.700
The Straw Hats would go straight through to
the new world with an overpowered Luffy leading

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.190
them forward.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.049
Fishman island would be a breeze.

00:18:17.049 --> 00:18:21.679
There would probably be no need to team up
with the warlord Trafalgar Law at Punk Hazard,

00:18:21.679 --> 00:18:26.410
though they would likely still rescue Momonsoke
and Kin’emon, the samurai from Wano.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:32.450
Dressrosa would be no contest as Luffy would
easily topple Doflamingo from his puppet throne.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:38.510
However, not everything would be this easy,
particularly for the rest of the crew.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:44.740
Since there was no timeskip, Zoro, Sanji and
other straw hats would be incredibly underdeveloped

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.260
as they never had two years to train.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:53.190
If they were to be attacked by basically any
powerful enemy in the New World, Luffy would

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:58.049
need to save them all because they would not
be strong enough to protect themselves [show

00:18:58.049 --> 00:19:00.650
rest of the straw hats being overwhelmed by
other characters.

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:01.650
King, Queen, Katakuri, Cracker, etc…]

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:04.770
Another interesting question is how would
the other Emperors react to Luffy’s power

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:05.799
in the New World?

00:19:05.799 --> 00:19:09.070
They certainly wouldn’t underestimate him
again.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:13.830
But would Kaido join forces with the clear
inheritor of the Joy Boy title?

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:18.820
Or would he and Big Mom team up even earlier
to search for the One Piece?

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:22.940
However it happens, the race to find Laugh
Tale would certainly start much sooner in

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:23.940
the story.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:24.940
Let me know what you think would happen in
the comments below.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.659
And while Luffy’s incredible powers might
be enough to bring the Straw Hats through

00:19:27.659 --> 00:19:32.440
Whole Cake Island and Wano, it is equally
possible some of the straw hats could be defeated

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.150
or even killed.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:39.090
One other factor is that if the war at Marineford
was successful, Luffy may never have matured

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:41.580
beyond where he was pre-timeskip.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:45.920
The crushing defeat at the original Marineford
almost destroyed Luffy.

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:53.559
It forced him to grow up and train so that
he could be strong enough to protect his friends.

00:19:53.559 --> 00:19:59.210
If none of that happened, then seventeen year
old Luffy could still be too immature and

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:01.810
eventually lead his crew into trouble later
in the story.

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:05.419
And this leaves us with another super interesting
question.

00:20:05.419 --> 00:20:10.059
We saw that Gear 5 Luffy was able to save
Ace in the all out war at Marineford.

00:20:10.059 --> 00:20:14.049
And this would likely make him the World Government's
number one target.

00:20:14.049 --> 00:20:20.809
So we have to ask, what if Luffy was eventually
captured by the world government and set to

00:20:20.809 --> 00:20:22.900
be executed just like Ace?

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.820
Who would come to save HIM?

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:29.940
In other words, what would happen if Luffy
was going to be executed by the marines?

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.040
Shanks for watching.

